---
title: "get_deposit_signature GET /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/signature (Legion Backend API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: api_key = headers["x-api-key"]
    q_auth --> q_check_key: api_key valid
    q_check_key --> q_sign: identifier = round_id or user_context
    q_check_key --> q_reject: api_key invalid
    q_reject --> [*]: revert "unauthorized"
    q_sign --> q_compute_sig: request_sig = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, identifier)
    q_compute_sig --> q_send: GET /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/signature with X-Signature
    q_send --> q_parse: response = server_response
    q_parse --> q_success: response.status == 2xx
    q_parse --> q_no_application: user has no approved application
    q_parse --> q_error: response.status == other error
    q_success --> q_extract: deposit_sig = response.body.signature
    q_extract --> [*]: return deposit_signature
    q_no_application --> [*]: revert "no approved application"
    q_error --> [*]: revert "signature generation failed"

    note right of q_extract
        INV-001: deposit signature is cryptographic proof authorizing on-chain fund deposit
        INV-002: signature should be single-use or bound to specific deposit parameters
        INV-003: user must have an approved application before requesting deposit signature
        INV-004: replay of deposit signature could allow unauthorized deposits if not nonce-protected
    end note
